@startuml Deal Management Application - System Context

' Define the styles
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #e3f2fd
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #1976d2
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #fff3e0
skinparam actorBorderColor #f57c00
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #f3e5f5
skinparam databaseBorderColor #7b1fa2

' Title
title Deal Management Application - System Context Diagram (C4 Level 1)

' Actors
actor "Sales Representative" as salesrep <<Person>> #fff3e0
actor "Sales Manager" as manager <<Person>> #fff3e0
actor "System Administrator" as admin <<Person>> #fff3e0

' System
rectangle "Deal Management\nApplication" as system <<Software System>> #e3f2fd {
}

' External Systems
database "H2 Database" as db <<External System>> #f3e5f5

' Relationships
salesrep --> system : Creates and manages\nsales deals
manager --> system : Reviews deals and\nperformance metrics
admin --> system : Manages users and\nsystem configuration

system --> db : Stores deals, users,\nand transactions

' Notes explaining the context
note right of salesrep
  <b>Sales Representative</b>

  Primary users who:
  • Create new deals
  • Update deal status
  • Track pipeline
  • Close won deals
  • Manage deal products
end note

note right of manager
  <b>Sales Manager</b>

  Managers who:
  • Monitor team performance
  • Review all deals
  • Analyze sales metrics
  • Approve large deals
  • Generate reports
end note

note left of system
  <b>Deal Management Application</b>

  Core system that provides:
  • RESTful API for deal operations
  • Business rule validation
  • Deal lifecycle management
  • Query and filtering capabilities
  • Sample data for testing

  <b>Technology:</b>
  • Java 21 with Jakarta Servlets
  • Embedded Tomcat server
  • Layered architecture
  • Repository pattern

  <b>Key Features:</b>
  • CRUD operations for deals
  • Status-based filtering
  • Sales rep assignment
  • Product line items
  • Deal value calculation
end note

note right of db
  <b>H2 Database</b>

  Embedded relational database:
  • File-based persistence
  • JDBC connectivity
  • Schema auto-initialization
  • Web console for queries

  <b>Stores:</b>
  • Deal records
  • User accounts
  • Deal products
  • Audit information

  <b>Location:</b>
  ./data/commissions.mv.db
end note

' System boundary note
note bottom of system
  <b>System Boundary</b>

  The Deal Management Application is a standalone
  software system that runs as an embedded web server.

  It exposes HTTP/REST endpoints and stores data in
  an embedded database for simplicity and portability.

  This is a Level 1 (System Context) diagram showing
  the system's relationship with users and external systems.
end note

legend right
  <b>C4 Model - Level 1: System Context</b>

  Shows the big picture of the system landscape.

  <b>Purpose:</b>
  Provides a high-level view of how the Deal Management
  Application fits into its environment, showing:
  • Who uses the system (actors/users)
  • What the system does (core purpose)
  • External dependencies (database)

  <b>Audience:</b>
  • Technical and non-technical stakeholders
  • Project managers
  • Business analysts
  • Architects

  <b>Key Elements:</b>
  • Person (users of the system)
  • Software System (the application itself)
  • External System (dependencies)
  • Relationships (interactions)

  <b>Scope:</b>
  Everything in scope for the Deal Management
  Application, from a bird's-eye view.
endlegend

@enduml